{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor systematically assessed current danger signs, explained the case-scoped risk, clarified the inpatient timeline, addressed medication execution risk, built an executable plan with owner/timing/materials/fallback, and navigated the privacy barrier to obtain minimum safety information. No serious or minor responsibility-chain error is present. Five dimensions are at least good, and the model actively triggered and completed HO1 (reconstructed the staged care timeline) and HO2 (navigated the privacy barrier with practical alternatives). Both high-order points have meaningful trajectory impact and are supported by distinct evidence not used solely for minimum RC duties. The closure is safe, executable, traceable, and valid_closure.",
